  "body": "Stack order: #1005 (`issue/894-thread-mill`) -> #1045 (`issue/992-thread-undrilled`) -> this PR. #1005 and #1045 have merged to main (f0c316ff, 07cb331f); this PR now stands on main alone (merged at 36035af8). Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe Thread operation cuts external threads on a boss.\n\n- **`external` on the operation.** `OpParams::Thread { external }`: the list then holds bosses (`radius` = major radius, `entry_z` = top, `floor_z` = shoulder). File / MCP key `external`, additive, written only when set; the stamp digests it only when set, so no internal thread goes Stale.\n- **Boss recognition.** `drilling::recognize_bosses`: the hole recogniser's weld, circle fit and rim-span law with the facing vote inverted (closed round upright walls facing away from their axis). Stepped walls are never folded. Detect holes (button and MCP `detect_holes`) reads bosses when the operation is external. The Thread page gets \"External thread (on a boss)\", \"Detect bosses\" and a per-row Remove (a round base is a boss too).\n- **Judging a tool beside a boss, without the silhouette** (`operation::thread_boss`):\n  - crest law: tangency against each boss's MINOR circle (major less 0.6134 x pitch), nothing else in the region. The drawn wall is not what the crests answer to, so a matched thread is not convicted on every helix (the #1071 flaw, not repeated);\n  - root law: the solid law with the cutter narrowed by the EXTERNAL depth (`thread_op::root_cutter`, external threads only): roots, tip, shank, holder against the whole part, shoulder included. A boss gets no bore grant (`thread_op::bores` is empty for it), so the grant and a narrowed cutter are never stacked; internal threads use #1005's #1071 laws (`major_rims` + the thread grant) unchanged;\n  - neighbour law (new): the crest ring at full radius over the cutting length against every facet that is not the threaded boss's own wall, gouge tolerance only. The boss a run of feeds threads is read from the helix's own centre, never from nearness.\n- **Air law** (`thread_entry::judge_bosses`, #992's external analogue): every position the feeds take the tool through is read in the stock the program ahead leaves; a column under the tool's disc, more than one cell outside the boss, standing above the tip refuses the thread by name (place, heights, how far out and how deep to clear). Unknown prior is refused.\n- **Round-boss law** (`thread_boss::not_round`): a boss whose wall is not a tessellated circle (a hex stud, a square post) is refused at generate by name - \"the boss at (x, y) is not round - external thread milling needs a round boss\". The crest law and the neighbour law both take the boss wall for a circle, so a polygon's flats would be cut unjudged. Same sagitta test as the internal side's `walls_round` (`verify::hole_is_round`), on the boss wall.\n- **Door** (create / edit / retool, again at generate): a boss no thicker than the thread is deep; a thread longer than the mill reaches beside a boss (shank wider than the tooth roots, or the holder); infeed against the external depth.\n- **Simulation.** An external thread is swept at its external root radius (`thread_op::sim_radius`); the internal depth read 0.07 x pitch of the boss as cut and the post gate called it a gouge. Internal threads and taps unchanged.\n- The kernel ride is used as #1005 pinned it; nothing in #1005 / #1045 was reworked. No bugs found in them.\n\n## Sources\n\nISO 68-1 / ISO 965-1 / DIN 13 (external design root 17/24 H = 0.6134 P); Machinery's Handbook, \"Thread milling\"; Smid, \"CNC Programming Handbook\", thread milling chapter; Sutherland-Hodgman clipping and point-to-polygon distance (O'Rourke). No HSMWorks / Fusion material consulted. Decisions: `docs/decisions/985-external-threads.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `crates/app/tests/thread_boss.rs` (12 tests): `a_hex_stud_is_no_round_boss_and_is_refused_by_name`, `an_external_m8_thread_verifies_clean_and_posts_helical_moves` (generator verdict, post gate and program sim clean; G02 with Z; goldens), `a_single_form_mill_threads_an_m10_boss_one_turn_per_thread`, `left_hand_and_conventional_external_threads_verify_clean_too`, `detect_reads_the_bosses_of_an_external_thread_and_holes_of_an_internal_one`, `a_boss_standing_in_uncut_stock_is_refused_by_name`, `a_part_wall_the_roughing_left_standing_in_the_sweep_is_refused`, `a_wall_inside_the_crest_rings_sweep_is_a_gouge_that_blocks_the_post`, `impossible_bosses_are_refused_when_the_operation_is_made`, `a_hole_list_read_as_bosses_never_passes_silently`, `moving_the_roughing_after_the_thread_marks_it_stale_and_refuses_it`, `the_external_flag_edits_undoes_and_round_trips_the_project_file`.\n- Unit: `operation::thread_boss::tests` (7), `operation::thread_entry::tests` (3 new), `operation::thread_op::tests::an_external_thread_narrows_the_roots_by_the_external_depth`, `drilling::boss::tests` (4).\n- MCP: `mcp::external_thread_milling_over_the_tools`. UI: `thread_mill_page_tests::the_geometry_tab_switches_between_holes_and_bosses_and_apply_undoes`, `a_listed_feature_can_be_removed_from_the_draft`.\n- Goldens: `thread_mill_external_m8_multi_form.cl`, `nc/thread_mill_external_m8_multi_form.nc`, `thread_mill_external_m10_single_form.cl`.\n- Gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green on 29e097c9 (refreshed #1045 @ 6dd3f773 + main @ 683802be: tools 4s, sim 21s, motion 155s, app 842s, ui 30s; 17.6 min, 0 failed); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-tools --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. Thread suites run one by one: thread_mill 8, thread_mill_rim 11, thread_boss 12, thread_entry 5, hole_wall_flats 5, solid_law_goldens 7 (posted_gates/thread), coarse_rims 5, lib `thread` 18, mcp thread/fill_openings 3 - all green. Final head 4f15b9b3 adds only a clean merge of main @ 36035af8 (MCP tools, #1005/#1045 merges); thread suites and the mcp suite re-run green on it, clippy app+ui clean.\n\n## Not exercised / left open\n\n- A polygonal boss (hex stud, square post) is refused, not threaded; threading over flats is left for a follow-up if asked for.\n- No viewport pick of a boss: recognition plus Remove only. Follow-up #1132.\n- A near-net or cast stock with nothing machined ahead is refused (as a cored hole is under #992). Posed (3+2) external threads are refused.\n- The simulation does not draw the thread form; the boss shows at its drawn diameter.\n- The neighbour law walks the facets the path's box reaches with no spatial index; not timed on a large model.\n- No real machine run; NC checked by the golden and the Fanuc post only.\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp.rs` (already over 400 lines) grew by one test; the camcraft-mcp skill text is not updated (process file).\n- MCP: covered by the existing `add_operation` / `edit_operation` / `detect_holes` tools; no new tool.\n\nChangelog: Thread milling cuts external threads on a boss: an External option with boss detection, refusals by name for a boss too thin, a thread past the mill's reach and stock left standing around the boss (#985)\nEffort: max (no escalation)\n\nFixes #985\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
